<title>USA: Sepracor sees June asthma drug NDA filing.</title>
<headline>Sepracor sees June asthma drug NDA filing.</headline>
<dateline>MARLBOROUGH, Mass. 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sepracor Inc said Tuesday it expects to file a New Drug Application for its asthma drug levalbuterol by June 30.</p>
<p>Sepracor said levalbuterol appears to have fewer side effects and longer duration that albuterol products Ventolin, manufactured by Glaxo Wellcome Plc, and Proventil, made by Schering-Plough Corp.</p>
<p>&quot;We believe that our Phase III pivotal study and pediatric trials will enable us to demonstrate reduced cardiac stimulation, reduced tremor and longer duration with comparable efficacy,&quot; Sepracor said in a press release.</p>
</text>
